    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Commercial-Sites/Early-Childhood-Teacher_JR-018601-1": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Teacher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking an outstanding Early Childhood Teacher to join our team in a unique, exceeding University Centre.   The right person will (for all, internal and external) Be inspired by children’s thinking, and passionate about Arts Education, Indigenous Perspectives and Learning in Nature Hold a deep understanding of Inquiry curriculum, and be skilled at planning, leading and documenting inquiry-based learning Be a team person who is dedicated to contributing to the ongoing growth of a high-achieving Centre Position Number: JR-018601  Role type:  Full-Time, Continuing (Multiple roles available)  Location: Abbotsford  Department/ School: Student and Scholarly Services; Chief Operating Officer Portfolio  Salary: UoM 5 - $86,943 - $99,864 p.a. plus 17% super  Join our committed and experienced team as an Early Childhood Educator Teacher and contribute to providing a quality education in a leading early learning Centre.    Is this the perfect opportunity for you? Apply today ! Including the following documents:   Resume    Letter of Application outlining your interest and experience leading an inquiry curriculum grounded in:    Indigenous Perspectives    Learning in Nature    Arts Education   The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity   You will design and deliver exemplary early childhood education programmes that align with national and Victorian frameworks. You will lead and mentor educators, partner closely with families, and support funded kindergarten delivery within a University-based service.  What you will deliver:    Design, implement and evaluate developmentally appropriate early childhood education programmes aligned with national and Victorian frameworks.  Lead, supervise and mentor educators in your team to ensure consistent, high-quality pedagogy and practice.  Observe, assess and document children’s learning, including developmental reports, parent–teacher interviews and transition statements.  Partner with families through clear, respectful communication about children’s progress, needs and learning experiences.  Ensure compliance with National Quality Standards, Education and Care legislation and Victorian Government kindergarten requirements.  You may be a great fit if you: Hold an approved early childhood teaching degree meeting ACECQA, DET and National Regulations requirements. Maintain current VIT registration, a Working with Children Check and HLTAID012 First Aid, including anaphylaxis and asthma. Apply strong knowledge of National Quality Standards, Education and Care Regulations and child-safe standards. Design and deliver play-based, inclusive and anti-bias early childhood programmes for children up to school entry. Lead and support educator teams, providing guidance, feedback and reflective pedagogical leadership. Communicate effectively with families and colleagues, using sound written, oral and basic information technology skills. For further information, please refer to the attached PD.   What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – Student and Scholarly Services    You will join Student and Scholarly Services within the Chief Operating Officer Portfolio, supporting the University’s youngest learners and their families. Early Childhood Education Services operates three centres that deliver high-quality education and care grounded in contemporary early childhood theory and practice. You will work with dedicated educators who value collaboration, inclusion and continuous improvement, and who are committed to exceeding National Quality Standards while supporting the broader University community.  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.   Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with Korin Korin, our Indigenous Employment and Development team, via korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.  Please upload a separate document addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description.  Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Helen Thomson at helen.thomson@unimelb.edu.au   For questions related to our recruitment process email Tien Nguyen at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close:  Tuesday, 3rd November 2026, at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:   PD_JR-005612 Early Childhood Teacher.docx   PD_JR-005612 Early Childhood Teacher.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Clinical-Sites-Metro--Regional/Assistant-Clinical-Trials-Manager--Maternal-Fetal-Medicine_JR-018776": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Trials Manager, Maternal Fetal Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nRole type:  0.8 – 1 FTE; Fixed-term until 31 December 2027 Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences Department/ School:  Obstetrics, Gynaecology and Newborn Health                     Location: Western Health, Sunshine Hospital Salary: $100,847 - $109,163 p.a. pro rata for part-time plus 17% superannuation Impact maternal and childhood health through C*STEROID and PRECeDe / coordinate multi-site trials / collaborate with maternity researchers The PRECeDe Trial The C*STEROID Trial – University of Auckland  Bring your clinical trials expertise to maternal fetal medicine and help transform evidence-based care for families Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will play a central role coordinating large, international maternal fetal medicine trials and long-term childhood follow-up studies. Working closely with the Clinical Trials Manager, you will oversee multi-site operations, data quality and trial processes. You will help generate evidence that improves outcomes for mothers, babies and children in Australia and beyond. What you will deliver:   Support ethics and governance submissions, site assessments and contracts to enable timely trial start-up across all sites. Coordinate day-to-day operations for C*STEROID, PRECeDe and related studies, ensuring adherence to protocols and GCP standards. Lead data management activities, including database design, training site staff, data cleaning, integrity checks and data locking. Liaise with over twenty recruiting sites, investigators and trial teams to support recruitment, workflow and issue resolution. Contribute to stakeholder communications and oversight through meeting coordination, reports, consumer engagement and long-term follow-up planning.   You may be a great fit if you:   Hold postgraduate qualifications in science, allied health, nursing, medicine or public health, or equivalent experience and training. Bring substantial experience in clinical trials, including multi-site hospital research governance, coordination and project management. Demonstrate strong knowledge of ICH GCP, NHMRC clinical trial policies and international research governance requirements. Use Office applications confidently, and manage databases such as REDCap to support accurate, high-quality trial data. Write clear ethics applications, reports and correspondence, and communicate complex trial information effectively to diverse stakeholders. Manage competing deadlines with excellent organisation, attention to detail, professionalism and independence within a collaborative team. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave, cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – Join the Western Health Maternal Fetal Medicine Research Unit, partnering with the University of Melbourne. The team in Obstetrics, Gynaecology and Newborn Health leads landmark MRFF- and NHMRC-funded trials, including C*STEROID and PRECeDe. You will support pregnancy research and long-term childhood follow-up studies with national collaborators. You will work with clinicians, researchers, statisticians and trial coordinators in a supportive environment valuing integrity and teamwork. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Prof Joanne Said by emailing For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Wednesday the 4th of November 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-018776 - Assistant Clinical Trials Manager, Maternal Fetal Medicine - PD.docx JR-018776 - Assistant Clinical Trials Manager, Maternal Fetal Medicine - PD"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Cybersecurity-Advisory-Manager_JR-018711-1": {
      "title": "Cybersecurity Advisory Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Continuing Department/ School:  Chief Information Officer Group, Cybersecurity  Salary: UOM 10 $156,480 p.a. plus 17% superannuation, negotiable commensurate with qualifications and experience, a loading sum may be applied to the salary offered. Strategic leadership of University-wide cyber advisory / shape secure, modern technology solutions / coach a specialist high-performing team Join us to lead cyber advisors and drive secure, innovative technology outcomes across the University. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities .  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead a specialist cybersecurity advisory team shaping secure, modern technology decisions University-wide.  You will influence strategy, eliminate legacy risk, and uplift resilience across teaching, research and operations.   What you will deliver:   Lead and coach cybersecurity advisors, managing workload and priorities based on risk and business impact. Direct cybersecurity advisory engagements, aligning recommendations with university priorities and delivering practical, risk-based outcomes. Provide expert guidance on technology designs, mitigation strategies, and project delivery, translating risks into actionable advice. Identify emerging threats and vulnerabilities, driving continuous improvement towards secure, fit-for-purpose solutions and practices. Collaborate with cybersecurity leadership and senior stakeholders to shape roadmap, embed security and modernise legacy technologies. You may be a great fit if:   Hold postgraduate qualifications in cybersecurity or an equivalent, highly relevant professional certification. Demonstrate extensive leadership experience across complex cybersecurity initiatives within large, multi-stakeholder organisations. Apply deep knowledge of cloud, network, identity and data security, using frameworks like ISO27001 and NIST. Lead proactive identification and mitigation of cyber risks and vulnerabilities, strengthening organisational resilience and readiness. Drive innovation by retiring legacy technologies and championing secure, contemporary solutions aligned with business needs. Communicate complex cybersecurity concepts clearly to diverse stakeholders, building trusted relationships and influencing decisions. For further information please refer to the attached PD’s at the bottom of the advert.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation. Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!    Your new team – Chief Information Officer Group   You will join the Chief Information Officer Group, the University’s integrated IT function enabling education and research. Cybersecurity sits at the heart of this portfolio, preventing, detecting and responding to threats across campus. You will collaborate with passionate experts, drive innovation, and strengthen secure digital experiences for students and staff. Be Yourself The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Alex Spezza at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Wednesday the 4th of November 2026 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-018711 - Cybersecurity Advisory Manager - UOM 10 PD.docx JR-018711 - Cybersecurity Advisory Manager - UOM 10 PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Research-Fellow--Carbon-Mineralization_JR-019399-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow, Carbon Mineralization",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed-Term for 18 Months  Faculty: Faculty of Science  Department/ School: School of Geography, Earth and Atmospheric Sciences Salary: Level A: $87,266 - $118,416 p.a. plus 17% super (PhD entry level $110,319 p.a.)    Innovative net zero research combining hands-on DAC-MIN pilot plant experimentation and modelling.  Join a world-class team advancing carbon mineralisation technologies to support Australia's transition to a net zero future.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.       The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity   In this role, you will drive experimental and modelling research to advance ex situ carbon mineralisation technologies. You will operate and optimise a pioneering DAC-MIN pilot plant, applying scientific expertise to help develop practical solutions for reducing carbon emissions.  What you will deliver:    Design and conduct laboratory experiments and geochemical modelling to advance ex situ carbon mineralisation processes.  Develop and refine methods for cation leaching, impurity removal, and carbonate precipitation from industrial waste materials.  Operate, monitor and optimise the carbon mineralisation pilot plant, ensuring safe, efficient, and reliable performance.  Publish high-impact research, present at conferences, and contribute to competitive funding proposals and industry partnerships.  Co-supervise and mentor graduate and PhD students, supporting a collaborative, inclusive research culture within the School.  You may be a great fit if you:    Hold, or be near completing, a PhD in hydrogeochemistry, industrial chemistry, chemical engineering, or related discipline.  Demonstrate research experience in fluid–rock reactions, carbon mineralisation, or water treatment, including experimental or modelling work.  Present a strong, peer-reviewed publication record in relevant fields, commensurate with career stage and opportunities.  Bring proven project or laboratory management skills, ensuring safe, efficient delivery of complex experimental programmes.  Collaborate effectively in multi-disciplinary teams and communicate complex concepts clearly to diverse academic and industry stakeholders.  Contribute to student supervision, mentoring, and the development of competitive research funding applications and collaborations.  For further information please refer to the attached PD.   What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program     For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – School of Geography, Earth and Atmospheric Sciences   Joining the School of Geography, Earth and Atmospheric Sciences, you will work within a vibrant, multi-disciplinary community.  The School unites strengths in geography, geoscience and atmospheric science, with leading expertise in climate change, environmental hazards and Earth system interactions.  As part of the Faculty of Science, you will access world-class facilities, diverse research networks and strong industry partnerships. You will be supported by an inclusive culture that values Indigenous knowledge, collaboration and impactful science for a better future.  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  This role is eligible for visa sponsorship and we welcome international applicants. If successful, we will support you through this process .   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria     Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Prof. Ralf Haese at ralf.haese@unimelb.edu.au    For questions related to our recruitment process email Oliver Bukasa at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').     Apply today and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close: 19 November 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:   JR-019399 - Research Fellow, Carbon Mineralization - PD.docx JR-019399 - Research Fellow, Carbon Mineralization - PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Academic-Support-Officer_JR-019220": {
      "title": "Academic Support Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nRole type:  Part Time (0.6FTE); Fixed term for 2 years Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences Department/ School:  Department of Psychiatry; Melbourne Medical School Salary: UOM 5 - $86,943 - $99,864 p.a. pro-rata for part time plus 17% super  Impact psychiatry training programs, systems and event coordination / supportive, values-driven academic and professional team Apply now to shape psychiatry education, support trainee psychiatrists, and grow your expertise in academic administration. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will support flagship psychiatry training programmes, ensuring seamless course administration and an excellent student experience. You will collaborate closely with academic and clinical stakeholders, manage digital platforms, and contribute to continuous improvement in teaching delivery. What you will deliver:   Provide high-level administrative support for course promotion, preparation, timetabling, and correspondence. Maintain and update Canvas subjects, enrolments, and weekly class setup to ensure smooth online delivery. Monitor and manage student fees using Magento and collect participation and funding data for reporting. Coordinate teaching-related events, including annual awards, and induct supervisors and students in systems and technology. Contribute to continuous improvement in course delivery and support the education team across daily operations.   You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a relevant tertiary qualification or equivalent combination of education, training, and administrative experience. Demonstrate strong organisational and time management skills, with proven ability to manage competing deadlines. Apply high-level communication skills to build effective relationships with diverse stakeholders. Use learning management systems, Zoom videoconferencing, and Microsoft Office confidently to support teaching and administration. Understand privacy, confidentiality, and data management principles within an educational context, including accurate record-keeping. Showcase initiative and problem-solving ability, contributing to process improvements and responsive student-centred service. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave, cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – You will join a dedicated team delivering psychiatry education for trainee psychiatrists. The team collaborates across teaching, research, and student support, guided by compassionate, respectful, collaborative values. You will work with experienced clinicians, educators, and professional staff who value initiative and improvement. Together you will contribute to developing the mental health workforce through excellent education and student support. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Lina Pepe by emailing linap@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 3rd of November 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-019220 - Academic Support Officer - PD.pdf JR-019220 - Academic Support Officer - PD.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Shepparton-Victoria/Deputy-Director-Of-Medical-Student-Education---Wangaratta_JR-019065": {
      "title": "Deputy Director Of Medical Student Education - Wangaratta",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nRole type:  1x Part Time (0.5FTE) or 2x 0.25 FTE positions; Fixed Term for 3 years Faculty: Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences; Department/ School:  Department of Rural Health; Melbourne Medical School Location: Green Street, Wangaratta Salary: Level C: $152,695 - $176,065 p.a. pro-rata for part time plus 17% super  Shape rural medical education in Wangaratta / build strong clinical and community partnerships / support and mentor medical students Apply now to lead rural clinical teaching, champion student support, and strengthen partnerships across the Regional Clinical School. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead rural clinical medical education for RCS students based at Northeast Health Wangaratta. You will oversee curriculum delivery, support students academically and pastorally, and contribute to research and professional engagement. What you will deliver:   Collaborate with Northeast Health Wangaratta’s Medical Education Team to align and continually improve the RCS curriculum. Oversee organisation, delivery, and administration of the RCS curriculum, including student assessment processes and documentation. Provide high quality clinical teaching plus regular pastoral and academic support for Wangaratta based RCS students. Work with DDMSEs across Ballarat, Echuca, and Shepparton to coordinate student movements between Clinical School nodes. Engage in departmental, community, and professional activities, including conferences, seminars, and appropriate research supervision.   You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a medical qualification recognised in Australia plus Fellowship of an Australian College or equivalent postgraduate degree. Work clinically within the Wangaratta region and maintain national standing through involvement in relevant professional bodies. Demonstrate substantial experience teaching medical students, including clinical teaching, curriculum delivery, and course coordination. Possess strong interpersonal and communication skills enabling collaborative relationships with clinicians and health professionals across settings. Show clear understanding of regional hospital environments in Victoria and willingness to engage with university systems and procedures. Demonstrate leadership capability within medical education, including taking responsibility in teaching and learning environments. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave, cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – You will join the Department of Rural Health within the Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences. Based at Wangaratta Clinical School, the team delivers high quality rural clinical education across multiple Victorian communities. The department values collaboration, compassion, respect, integrity, and accountability, fostering innovation and supportive development for staff and students.   Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Steven Bismire by emailing steven.bismire@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 2 November 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-019065 Deputy Director Of Medical Student Education - Wangaratta PD.docx JR-019065 Deputy Director Of Medical Student Education - Wangaratta PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Clinical-Sites-Metro--Regional/Senior-Lecturer--Surgery--Wangaratta-_JR-019025": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, Surgery (Wangaratta)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nRole type:  Part-time (0.2 FTE); Fixed-term to 31 December 2028 Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences Department/ School:  Department of Rural Health; Melbourne Medical School Location: Green Street, Wangaratta Salary: Level C: $152,695 - $176,065 p.a. pro rata for part time plus 17% super Senior rural surgical education role / shape clinical learning with Northeast Health Wangaratta / combine teaching, leadership and research Join us to lead rural surgical teaching and mentor future surgeons in a collaborative regional clinical school. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead and coordinate high quality surgical teaching for Rural Clinical School students in Wangaratta. You will organise clinical placements, mentor students and collaborate closely with Northeast Health Wangaratta teaching teams. You will also contribute to rural health research and departmental projects aligned with your surgical expertise. What you will deliver:   Deliver engaging small group tutorials, demonstrations and clinical teaching sessions in general surgery for RCS students. Coordinate student exposure to surgical clinics, ward rounds and inpatient experiences at Northeast Health Wangaratta. Oversee student orientation, supervision and assessment, including in-term tasks and mid and end-year examinations. Contribute to Rural Clinical School committees, educator meetings and projects that strengthen rural medical education and partnerships. Supervise medical student research projects and support grant applications and publications related to rural surgical practice.   You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a medical qualification recognised in Australia and Fellowship of an Australian College, or equivalent. Demonstrate substantial experience in clinical teaching, medical education and curriculum delivery within surgical settings. Build productive working relationships with surgeons, junior doctors and multidisciplinary teams in hospitals and community settings. Understand regional hospital systems and university processes and navigate them effectively to support students and colleagues. Exhibit strong organisational and administrative skills, managing multiple teaching commitments alongside clinical responsibilities. Commit to maintaining contemporary clinical and medical education skills through ongoing professional development. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave, cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – You will join the Department of Rural Health within the Melbourne Medical School, based at Wangaratta Clinical School. The team delivers high quality health professional education and research training focused on strengthening the rural health workforce. You will collaborate closely with Northeast Health Wangaratta and many regional partners across rural Victoria. The culture values innovation, collaboration, respect and continuous improvement in teaching, research and community engagement. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Steve Bismire by emailing steven.bismire@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 3 November 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-019025 Senior Lecturer, Surgery (Wangaratta) PD .docx JR-019025 Senior Lecturer, Surgery (Wangaratta) PD .pdf"
